rn Michigan after 13 seasons","description":"Chris Creighton is out as head coach at Eastern Michigan after 13 seasons with the school.","published":"2026-11-25T19:05:05.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50595706/creighton-coach-eastern-michigan-13-seasons","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Judge denies SEC's request for TRO against LSU in Dec. 3 vote","description":"A federal judge denied the SEC's request for a temporary restraining order to keep LSU from interfering with a Dec. 3 vote of presidents and chancellors on whether to remove the school from the conference.","published":"2026-11-25T20:02:54.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-sports/story/_/id/50595702/judge-denies-sec-request-tro-lsu-dec-3-vote","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079636/dom-nichols","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominic_Nichols"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Dominic Nichols","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dominic_Nichols","description":"American football player (born 2006)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:38:11Z","intro":"Dominic Nichols (born February 6, 2006) is an American football defensive end for the Michigan Wolverines.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Nichols attended Oakdale High School in Frederick, Maryland. He was rated as a four-star recruit by 247Sports and committed to play college football for the Michigan Wolverines over offers from Clemson, Kentucky, and Wisconsin."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"In the 2024 ReliaQuest Bowl, Nichols totaled two tackles and a forced fumble in an upset win over Alabama. As a freshman during the 2024 season, he played in five games, recording three tackles and a forced fumble. In 2025, Nichols notched 19 tackles with five and a half for a loss and a sack."}]}}